From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Mon, 9 Nov 2026 22:20:21 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: carry Telegram calls with tgcalls-lite alone, without
 libtgvoip

NoTgvoip=ON builds the call path on tgcalls-lite only: libtgvoip is
neither looked up nor linked, VoIPController is the empty stand-in, and
LUNEOS_TELEGRAM_CALL_ENGINE no longer selects libtgvoip.

We offer only tgcalls-lite's version, 7.0.0, which Telegram Desktop,
Android and iOS all register (tgcalls InstanceV2Impl). libtgvoip only
carried a call when the peer agreed on no version at all, which no
current official client does; such a peer is now told the call cannot
be carried, and the call is discarded. libtgvoip's echo cancellation,
noise suppression and gain control only ever applied on that path.

Without tgcalls-lite, NoTgvoip disables calls.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
---
